  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'The highest double is played first. On each player’s first turn, they must place a double as the engine in front of them; if someone cannot do this opening play, the hand is blocked and redealt. After the first turn, a player adds a matching tile to either end of their own train. After adding to their own train, they may add one tile to any or all other players’ trains. A player unable to extend their own train loses the turn. Doubles are played inline and do not create spinners.',
    Player: 'The highest double is played first. On each player’s first turn, they must place a double as the engine in front of them; if someone cannot do this opening play, the hand is blocked and redealt. After the first turn, a player adds a matching tile to either end of their own train. After adding to their own train, they may add one tile to any or all other players’ trains. A player unable to extend their own train loses the turn. Doubles are played inline and do not create spinners.',
    objective: 'Play all tiles from your hand or finish with the lowest pip total when play stops.',
    gameplay: 'The highest double is played first. On each player’s first turn, they must place a double as the engine in front of them; if someone cannot do this opening play, the hand is blocked and redealt. After the first turn, a player adds a matching tile to either end of their own train. After adding to their own train, they may add one tile to any or all other players’ trains. A player unable to extend their own train loses the turn. Doubles are played inline and do not create spinners.',
    keyRules: [
      'No boneyard is used; leftover tiles are out of play.',
      'Each player must start their personal train with a double on the first turn.',
      'A player must add to their own train before adding one tile to other players’ trains.',
      'Doubles are inline and do not branch.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Four to ten players. The rules table gives hand sizes for double-nine and double-twelve sets according to player count.',
      deck: 'A double-nine or double-twelve domino set. Leftover tiles are set aside face down and are not used as a boneyard.',
      equipment: 'Domino set and enough table space for each player to maintain a personal train.',
      dealing: 'Deal all playable hands according to player count; any leftover tiles are put aside face down and are not drawn during play.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'The highest double is played first. On each player’s first turn, they must place a double as the engine in front of them; if someone cannot do this opening play, the hand is blocked and redealt. After the first turn, a player adds a matching tile to either end of their own train. After adding to their own train, they may add one tile to any or all other players’ trains. A player unable to extend their own train loses the turn. Doubles are played inline and do not create spinners.',
