    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 13 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Play all tiles from your hand or finish with the lowest pip total when play stops.',
      'Turn-flow example: The highest double is played first. On each player’s first turn, they must place a double as the engine in front of them; if someone cannot do this opening play, the hand is blocked and redealt. After the first turn, a player adds a matching tile to either end of their own train. After adding to their own train, they may add one tile to any or all other players’ trains. A player unable to extend their own train loses the turn. Doubles are played inline and do not create spinners.',
      'Scoring example: When a player empties or the game stops, players score the pip totals left in hand; lower is better for the hand. Win by emptying your hand or by having the lowest remaining pip total when the hand is blocked..',
